  "abstract": {
    "value": "Abstract 2,3-Allenols, an important class of allenes containing a 1,2-propadiene unit and a hydroxy group, are highly reactive. The reactions of 2,3-allenols and their derivatives are reviewed. The reactions of 2,3-allenols include transition metal-catalyzed cycloisomerization reactions, Pd-catalyzed coupling reactions, ruthenium-catalyzed cyclic carbonylation reactions, ring expansion reactions, electrophilic addition reactions, cycloaddition reactions, and radical reactions. On the other hand, the reactions of the derivatives of 2,3-allenols are Pd(0)-catalyzed reactions involving methylene-<sup>π</sup>-allyl palladium intermediates forming allenes or 1,3-dienes regioselectively, $S _ { \\mathrm { N } } 2 '$ type addition-elimination reactions, Pd(II)-catalyzed intramolecular cyclizations and rearrangement reactions.",
    "source": "content_list_first_paragraph_after_authors",
    "confidence": 0.68,
